  },
  "object_storage": {
    "price_per_gb_monthly": 0.07,
    "egress_price_per_gb": 0,
    "currency": "EUR",
    "type": "S3-compatible (beta)",
    "notes": "Beta, FIN-03 only. EUR 0.07 per GiB-month (EUR 71.68/TiB); egress, ingress and API requests free (verda.com/object-storage). Default quotas 1 TiB, 100k objects, 100 buckets. Price is per GiB, not GB."
  },
  "notes": "Verda (formerly DataCrunch), Helsinki, Finland. GPU/AI cloud. Prices are Verda's own EUR list prices (verda.com/pricing?currency=eur and the public, unauthenticated instance-type endpoint api.verda.com/v1/instance-types?currency=eur), fetched 2026-11-01; no own currency conversion. Verda also publishes USD prices (price_usd_hourly); the EUR list equals USD x 0.8951, i.e. it tracks the ECB rate (1 EUR = 1.1172 USD on 2026-10-30), so EUR values may move with FX. Prices exclusive of VAT (T&C: fees charged 'together with applicable taxes'). On-demand (Pay As You Go) prices; billed in pre-paid 10-minute increments, price_monthly = hourly x 730. price_spot_hourly = published spot price (50% of on-demand for GPUs, 40% for CPU). The API exposes a dynamic_price field, but it was null for every type on 2026-11-01 (max_dynamic_price = on-demand price), so no dynamic pricing applied at fetch time. Reserved discounts on GPU instances: 1 month 2%, 3 months 3%, 6 months 4%, 1 year 8%, 2 years 25% off on-demand (paid up-front). Locations: FIN-01, FIN-02, FIN-03 (all Helsinki); pricing page and API do not differentiate by location, docs say prices can vary by location. GPU instances: 1x/2x/4x/8x as listed by the API (A100 40GB only 1x/8x, GB300 only 1x/2x/4x); vCPU/RAM as published. Not included: confidential-computing variants (GPU: 1x RTX PRO 6000 CC EUR 2.415/h, B200 CC from 2x EUR 16.19/h, B300 CC from 4x EUR 41.45/h; CPU .CC types about 2% above standard CPU), Instant Clusters (same per-GPU price as instances for GB300/B300/B200/H200, multi-node with InfiniBand, up to 144 GPUs self-service), Serverless containers (e.g. 1x H100 EUR 4.72/h). CPU instances: CPU-TURIN.* (AMD EPYC Turin) and CPU.* (AMD Rome/Milan, Genoa for 180V/360V) have identical prices. Instances have no included disk: OS and data volumes are NVMe block volumes billed per GiB. No managed Kubernetes for regular instances; Instant Clusters can be provisioned with a vanilla kubeadm-based Kubernetes orchestrator (no separate control-plane price published). No load balancer product or public IPv4 price published. Egress/traffic pricing for compute is not published; only Object Storage (beta) explicitly states free egress/ingress/requests."
}
